/**

@brief BL0.5 launcher
@defgroup tests_bl0p5_launch BL0.5 launcher
@ingroup all_tests
@details
The BL0.5 launcher (app/bl0p5/src/bl0p5_launch.c) runs the host handshake, checks the staged
BUN2 bundle, copies the SMC BL1 image to its load address, and jumps to it.

The tests run the real launcher on the host, on native_sim. The BUN2 staging area, the host boot
state and bundle validation registers, and the reset vector are RAM buffers. A pause hook plays
the host by writing the next scripted register value on each poll. The jump is an FFF fake, so
the launcher returns instead of transferring control.

@section tests_bl0p5_launch_scope Scope

Covered on the host:
- The handshake states the launcher writes and waits for.
- Bundle validation: TOC index 0 must be an SMC BL1 image.
- The copy of the BL1 image, the reset vector write, and the jump.

Not covered by these tests:
- The real jump into BL1, and what happens if BL1 returns. Those need the device.
- The host side of the handshake, which runs on the host over PCIe. The end-to-end device tests
  cover it and are not part of this group yet.
- Failure modes the launcher does not yet check. See the proposed checks below.

@section tests_bl0p5_launch_plan Test plan

| Test | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|
| test_announces_wait_for_bundle_first | Host state is WAIT_FOR_BUNDLE (1) on the first poll. |
| test_staged_check_masks_upper_bits | Only the low nibble of the host state is compared. 0x11 keeps waiting, 0x12 proceeds. |
| test_validation_requires_validated_bit | The READY bit alone does not complete validation. |
| test_valid_bundle_copies_bl1_and_jumps | Host state is CONSUMED before the copy. The image is in place at the jump. The reset vector and jump get the entry point. TOC entry 1 is not copied. |
| test_empty_bundle_returns_enoent | No TOC entries returns -ENOENT. No copy, no jump, host state stays STAGED. |
| test_wrong_type_at_index0_returns_enoent | An SMC BL0.5 image at index 0 returns -ENOENT, even with SMC BL1 at index 1. |
| test_bl1_at_later_index_is_not_used | A SEP BL1 image at index 0 returns -ENOENT, even with SMC BL1 at index 1. |
| test_staging_timeout_returns_etimedout | A host that never stages gets -ETIMEDOUT after max_polls polls. No copy, no jump, host state stays WAIT (1). |
| test_validation_timeout_returns_etimedout | A host that stages but never validates gets -ETIMEDOUT after max_polls validation polls. No copy, no jump, host state stays STAGED (2). |
| test_staging_on_last_allowed_poll_succeeds | Staging on poll max_polls is accepted, and the launcher jumps. |
| test_staging_one_poll_late_times_out | Staging one poll after the budget gives -ETIMEDOUT, with no copy and no jump. |

The test functions are documented in the source with the same descriptions.

@section tests_bl0p5_launch_proposed Proposed checks for the launcher

These are not implemented. Each one is a decision about the production code, so each needs
review before it changes:

1. Bounds on the staging area. Check that payload_offset is non-negative and inside the staging
   area, and that payload_offset + offset + length stays inside it, without overflow.
2. Bounds on load_addr. The copy must not overlap BL0.5's own image, its stack, the staging area,
   or the reset vector. Right now a bad load_addr can overwrite BL0.5 while it is running.
3. Entry point inside the image. Check that entry_point falls in [load_addr, load_addr + length).
4. Manifest version. Reject a manifest_version_major the launcher does not support.
5. A validation failure state. The validation register has no failure value, so the launcher
   can only wait for success.
6. main() should log the return value of bl0p5_launch() before k_panic(). Today the error is
   dropped silently.
7. Image integrity. TOC entries carry a 32-byte hash. The launcher does not check the copied
   image against it. Whether to check it here depends on what the hardware or BL1 already
   verifies, which is a question for the bundle owners.

*/
